GLOBAL RULE FOR ALL ANIMATIONS
==================================================

Do NOT redesign the existing UI when these prompts are reused.

The copied prompt for every animation must contain this instruction:

"Apply this motion system to the specified existing elements while preserving their current content, dimensions, typography, colors, styling, responsive behavior and functionality. Do not redesign or restructure the existing UI unless required for the animation wrapper."

Animation implementations must prioritize:

transform
translateX
translateY
translateZ
scale
rotate
rotateX
rotateY
opacity

Avoid expensive continuous animation of:

width
height
top
left
margin

Target smooth 60 FPS.

Support prefers-reduced-motion.

==================================================
SET 1 — ANIMATIONS 01–15
==================================================


01 — 3D COVERFLOW / CENTER FOCUS

TYPE:
3D Carousel

Create a cinematic center-focused Coverflow.

Five items can be visible:

[ far-left ][ left ][ ACTIVE ][ right ][ far-right ]

ACTIVE:

x: 0
scale: 1
rotateY: 0
translateZ: 0
opacity: 1

ADJACENT:

scale: approximately 0.85–0.9
rotateY: approximately ±8–12deg
translateZ: approximately -100px
opacity: 0.8–0.9

OUTER:

scale: approximately 0.7–0.78
rotateY: approximately ±15–20deg
translateZ: approximately -200px
opacity: 0.55–0.7

Core movement:

SIDE
→ FORWARD
→ SCALE UP
→ STRAIGHTEN
→ CENTER

while the previous center:

CENTER
→ SIDE
→ SHRINK
→ ROTATE
→ RECEDE

Support:

- arrows
- drag
- swipe
- click-to-focus
- keyboard
- infinite looping

Use perspective approximately 1200–1600px.


02 — STACK SLIDER

TYPE:
Stack / Depth

Cards should appear physically stacked behind the active card.

Front card:

scale: 1
translateY: 0
translateZ: 0

Cards behind progressively:

move upward/downward slightly
scale down
move deeper in Z-space
reduce opacity

Navigation:

FRONT CARD
→ slides outward
→ slightly rotates
→ fades
→ moves behind stack

NEXT CARD
→ moves forward
→ scales to 1
→ becomes active

Make it feel like cycling through a physical deck.


03 — FAN ROTATION

TYPE:
Fan / Radial

Cards originate around a shared lower pivot.

Inactive cards should fan outward using different rotations.

Example:

-24°
-12°
0°
12°
24°

The active card should move slightly forward and straighten.

On interaction:

collapsed stack
→ cards progressively rotate outward
→ spacing increases
→ fan opens

Reverse smoothly when closed.

Use transform-origin near bottom-center.


04 — VERTICAL PARALLAX

TYPE:
Parallax / Layered

Arrange cards in vertical depth layers.

During scrolling or interaction:

front layers move faster
middle layers move moderately
rear layers move slower

Combine:

translateY
translateZ
scale
opacity

Do not simply move all cards together.

Create genuine perceived depth.


05 — FLIP CAROUSEL

TYPE:
3D Flip

Cards transition through 3D Y-axis rotation.

Outgoing:

rotateY: 0 → approximately -90deg
translateZ decreases
opacity decreases

Incoming:

rotateY: approximately 90deg → 0
translateZ increases
opacity increases

Use:

perspective
transform-style: preserve-3d
backface-visibility

The animation must feel like physical cards rotating through space rather than a simple fade.


06 — INFINITE LOOP

TYPE:
Continuous Carousel

Create seamless horizontal card movement.

Cards continuously move:

RIGHT → LEFT

or configurable direction.

When an item leaves the viewport it should seamlessly re-enter from the opposite side.

There must be:

- no visible reset
- no teleportation
- no spacing jump

Support:

pause/slow on hover
dragging
responsive speed

Use duplicated track logic or mathematically wrapped positions.


07 — TILT & HOVER

TYPE:
Pointer Interactive

The element reacts to cursor position.

Map pointer position to:

rotateX
rotateY
translateZ

Example maximum:

rotateX: ±8deg
rotateY: ±10deg

Also dynamically move:

shadow
highlight
optional glare

Pointer leaves:

card returns smoothly to:

rotateX: 0
rotateY: 0
scale: 1

Use spring interpolation rather than directly attaching transforms to the pointer.


08 — EXPANDED CENTER

TYPE:
Focus Carousel

Center element becomes substantially more prominent.

CENTER:

scale: 1
opacity: 1

ADJACENT:

scale: 0.78–0.88
opacity: 0.65–0.85

When navigation occurs:

next card moves toward center
→ spacing changes
→ scale increases
→ shadow strengthens

Old center simultaneously contracts.

Avoid abrupt width changes; achieve visual expansion primarily through transforms.


09 — SCROLL TRIGGERED

TYPE:
Scroll Reveal

Use IntersectionObserver on the static showcase.

For reusable Framer Motion prompts use:

whileInView
viewport

Cards enter progressively.

Initial:

translateY: 40–80px
scale: approximately 0.94
opacity: 0

Final:

translateY: 0
scale: 1
opacity: 1

Use staggered children.

Do not make every card appear simultaneously.


10 — WAVE MOTION

TYPE:
Sequential / Wave

Cards form a horizontal composition.

Create a smooth wave traveling through the items.

Example:

card 1 rises
→ card 2 rises
→ card 3 rises
→ card 4 rises
→ card 5 rises

Previous cards simultaneously settle.

Use phase/timing offsets.

Combine subtle:

translateY
rotate
scale

Avoid cartoon-like bouncing.


11 — CUBE ROTATION

TYPE:
3D Structural

Cards should behave like surfaces positioned around a virtual 3D structure.

Navigation rotates the composition around the Y-axis.

Use:

perspective
rotateY
translateZ
preserve-3d

The next surface should naturally rotate into the front position.

Avoid faking the effect using only opacity.


12 — DEPTH LAYER

TYPE:
Z-Depth Stack

Arrange elements on different Z-depth planes.

ACTIVE:

translateZ: 0
scale: 1
opacity: 1

Each deeper layer:

translateZ progressively decreases
scale progressively decreases
opacity slightly decreases

Navigation moves the next layer physically forward.

Use depth and scale together to create strong spatial perception.


13 — MAGNETIC FOCUS

TYPE:
Pointer / Proximity

Cards react to pointer proximity rather than only direct hover.

As cursor approaches:

nearest card moves subtly toward pointer
scale increases slightly

Nearby cards receive weaker attraction.

Movement strength should be calculated from pointer distance.

Use spring smoothing.

Maximum movement must remain subtle.

The element must never feel attached directly to the cursor.


14 — CAROUSEL WITH PROGRESS

TYPE:
Controlled Carousel

Create a carousel with:

Previous
Next
Current slide
Total slides
Progress bar
Pagination dots

Example:

03 / 05

During navigation:

card transition and progress indicator animate together.

Progress should smoothly interpolate rather than instantly jump.


15 — 3D CURVED CARD FLOW

TYPE:
Curved 3D Carousel

Cards follow an invisible curved path.

CENTER:

x: 0
y: 0
scale: 1
rotateY: 0

Moving away from center:

x increases
y follows subtle curve
translateZ decreases
scale decreases
rotateY points toward center

The result should resemble cards positioned around part of a large invisible cylinder.

